--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI LifetimeStatsPage at web parity: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable
LifetimeStatsDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web LifetimeStats /
PersonalRecord / LifetimeAchievement 1:1 (production binds the shared KMP
repositories — useSelectedVehicle + useLifetimeStats, GET /analytics/lifetime
[vehicle_id] — through the seam). Every measurement is SI canonical on the model
(meters, meters/second, watt-hours); the view converts to the user's unit at the
render boundary via the shared Units facade (ADR-005). The page is the all-time
driving + charging + savings roll-up.

One lifetime query drives the page; its states switch in place (web PageContainer
loading/error + the per-panel `!stats` empties) — never a blank region. The hero +
four key tiles always render (zeros when `!stats`, exactly like the web hero /
StatCards); the six lower GlassPanels each show their own EmptyState when stats is
nil / the per-panel guard fails. The eleven web panels are reproduced:

  GlassPanel1  — Hero (LifetimeStatsPage.Hero.swift > LifetimeHeroPanel): the
                 SI-distance hero + "driven across N drives" + the optional
                 earthCompare / since lines.
  Total-Drives / Total-Distance / Total-Energy / Total-Savings — the four key
                 StatCards (LifetimeStatsPage.Hero.swift > LifetimeKeyStatsGrid +
                 LifetimeStatTile; the shared TSStatCard lacks unit/sublabel slots,
                 so a faithful tile composes TSCard + TSIconBox + typography).
  GlassPanel6  — Fun Facts        (LifetimeStatsPage.Sections.swift > LifetimeFunFactsPanel)
  GlassPanel7  — Savings vs Gas    (LifetimeSavingsPanel + Cards > LifetimeSavingsBar)
  GlassPanel8  — Environmental     (LifetimeEnvironmentalPanel — CO2 ring + trees + coffee)
  GlassPanel9  — Personal Records  (LifetimeRecordsPanel + Cards > LifetimeRecordCard)
  GlassPanel10 — Activity Summary  (LifetimeActivityPanel + Cards > LifetimeMiniStat)
  GlassPanel11 — Achievement Gallery (LifetimeAchievementsPanel + Cards > LifetimeAchievementBadge)

Adaptive (ADR-002/006): the hero, the stat/fun-fact grids, and the records/activity
rows reflow via adaptive LazyVGrid columns + the header's #if os(iOS) compact branch
(verified by the iOS whole-module type-check below). The pure web display logic was
ported 1:1 + unit-tested: fmtNumber (en-US grouping, fixed precision), fmtInt,
formatCurrency, fromKm/fromKmh (SI meters → user distance, SI m/s → user speed),
energy kWh from watt-hours, the Wh/km activity efficiency, the most-active-hour and
date formatting, and the derived coffeesSaved / unlockedAchievements / hasSavingsData.

Scope notes (no narrowing):
  - The web actions render <VehicleSelect /> (global selected vehicle) — reproduced as
    a header vehicle picker (TSSelect) that re-queries useLifetimeStats(vehicle_id),
    mirroring the sibling StatisticsPage; route.vehicles reused as its a11y label.
  - No live SSE / >2 min staleness indicator: the lifetime roll-up is cagg-driven
    (web staleTime SLOW + forceStaleAfterMs 6h), NOT a live source, so ADR-013 does
    not apply. (The web DataFreshnessAuto chip is a non-parity action, omitted.)
  - The opt-in <AILifetimeStatsQA /> block is a SEPARATE shared surface (already
    shipped under TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AILifetimeStatsQA*), not in this unit's
    parity record — not duplicated here.

Files (all new unless noted):
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsModels.swift             (SI value types / record / achievement / seam / phase)
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsFormat.swift             (display formatters via Units + date)
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsPageModel.swift          (@Observable model + vehicle select + reload)
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsPageModel.Sample.swift   (Sample/Empty/Failing sources + fixtures)
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsPage.swift               (chrome + header + 4 states + ready body)
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsPage.Hero.swift          (GlassPanel1 hero + 4 key tiles + LifetimeStatTile)
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsPage.Sections.swift      (GlassPanel6..11)
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsPage.Cards.swift         (FunFact/Savings/Record/MiniStat/Badge + skeleton)
  Sources/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsRouteRegistration.swift  (.lifetimeStats route)
  Tests/Unit/Features/Analytics/LifetimeStatsPageModelTests.swift  (state-machine + display-logic tests)
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift           (MOD: +.lifetimeStats case / "lifetime-stats" pathSegment / "trophy.fill" / Insights group)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift           (MOD: wire LifetimeStatsRouteRegistration into routeHostRegistry)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings   (MOD: +42 bare keys — 41 lifetime.* + route.lifetimeStats)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json        (MOD: +2 rows page:analytics/LifetimeStats 56/56 macos+ios)

Navigation: the web route /lifetime-stats resolves to the dedicated .lifetimeStats
route by its pathSegment ("lifetime-stats") via AppRouteParser's segment match —
reachable in the Insights sidebar group + deep-linkable, no alias needed. The
navigate-command catalog auto-covers it (MenuCommandCatalog.navigateCommands maps
AppRoute.allCases), and the generated TeslaSync.xcodeproj + built Frameworks/
Shared.xcframework are git-ignored.

